<a href="http://gangrey.com/1347">
<h2 class="design">Storming The News Gatekeepers</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">the citizen journalists</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2007/11/26/AR2007112602025.html">Jose Antonio Vargas</a>: NEW YORK -- Aboard the crowded D train, rumbling into Brooklyn on the Manhattan Bridge, the inevitable rant explodes. A rant courtesy of Faye Anderson, whom we'll call Ms. CJ, a.k.a. Citizen Journalist. A rant directed at us, Mr. MSM, a.k.a. Mainstream Media, for all our perceived faults. <br />
<br />
"It's not you, the journalist, it's the institution," Ms. CJ tells Mr. MSM. "You're not telling the whole story. . . . You've lost your credibility." <br />
<br />
We listen, take notes, check if the tape recorder's working. No telling what Anderson might do if she's misquoted. 
